Matrix nanocomposites are superior-performing substances with distinct features and design possibilities. Due to their exceptional thermophysical characteristics, they can be utilized in various applications ranging from packaging to biological uses. This groundbreaking work focuses on magnetized hybrid nanofluids disperse polymeric/ceramic matrix nanocomposites substances while flowing between orthogonal porous coaxial disks. The study also investigates the significance of the permeability value (

